            The <strong class="text-white">best plasma cutter</strong> for most home shops is the <strong class="text-white">Hypertherm Powermax30 XP</strong>: 3/8-inch rated cuts on 120 or 240 volts and consumables you can buy anywhere. Step up to the <strong class="text-white">Powermax45 XP</strong> or <strong class="text-white">Hobart AirForce 40i</strong> for 1/2-inch plate, and choose the <strong class="text-white">YesWelder CUT-55DS</strong> only if budget rules and you size it conservatively.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before you buy, check that your compressor can supply the flow at 90 psi, add an air filter, and plan for a 240-volt circuit if thicker cuts are routine. A cutter starved of air or current will disappoint, whatever the brand.
